   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Social and Political Rights of Persons with Disabilities in Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to provide co-financing to Action on Disability &amp; Development&apos;s European Council (EC)-funded programme to promote the rights of people with disabilities and help ensure their participation in elections in Bangladesh. It builds on Action on Disability &amp; Development&apos;s experience in mobilising voters, monitoring election work and supporting the actions of disabled people&apos;s organisations (DPOs) in ensuring the accountability of duty bearers.  

The project will target 13,473 people with disabilities and 1 million voters with and without disabilities in 41 upazilas of nine districts in Bangladesh over 2 years.  

Specifically, it will aim to: 

- empower citizens with disabilities and strengthen capacity of DPOs 
- promote obligation of Bangladesh to rights of people with disabilities; 
- improve awareness of PWDs for participation in the 10th Parliament Election;
- facilitate dialogue among political parties and other stakeholders to enhance political representation of people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
